Q: Hiding values of macro variables from libname statements A: <p>Note that the LIBNAME statement does NOT display the password in the LOG.  It will replace the password with XXXXX in the log.</p>
<p>You can use the macro processor to just reference the macro variable directly in your code.  If you are running the LIBNAME statement inside of a macro then make sure the also turn off the MPRINT option.</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>options nosymbolgen nomprint;

libname libref oracle
 user=&amp;user.
 password= &quot;&amp;pass&quot;
 path=&quot;path&quot;
 schema=schema
 connection=global
 defer=yes
;
</code></pre>
<p>You cannot use a function call in the LIBNAME statement.  And you cannot use the %SYSFUNC() macro function to call the SYMGET() function in macro code.</p>
<p>But you can use the LIBNAME() function if you use a data step.  That will reduce the messages about the LIBNAME definition in the SAS log.</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>data _null_;
  rc=libname('libref',,'oracle'
     ,catx(' ',&quot;user=&amp;user schema=schema connection=global defer=yes&quot;
       ,&quot;password='&amp;pass'&quot;)
     );
run;
</code></pre>
<p>Inside of that data step you could use the SYMGET() function which would hide the value of the macro variable without having to use the NOSYMBOLGEN system option. Just replace the</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>&quot;password='&amp;pass'&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>with</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>cats('password=',quote(symget('pass'),&quot;'&quot;))
</code></pre>

Q: React + Spring Boot Connectivity A: <h2>Basic Example: Fetching Data Properly</h2>
<h3>Key rules</h3>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>State holds data, loading, and error</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong><code>useEffect</code> runs side effects (fetching)</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Abort fetch on unmount</strong> (important!)</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Type your data</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>import { useEffect, useState } from &quot;react&quot;;

type User = {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
};

function Users() {
  const [users, setUsers] = useState&lt;User[]&gt;([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState&lt;boolean&gt;(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState&lt;string | null&gt;(null);

  useEffect(() =&gt; {
    const controller = new AbortController();

    const fetchUsers = async () =&gt; {
      setLoading(true);
      setError(null);

      try {
        const response = await fetch(
          &quot;https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users&quot;,
          { signal: controller.signal }
        );

        if (!response.ok) {
          throw new Error(&quot;Failed to fetch users&quot;);
        }

        const data: User[] = await response.json();
        setUsers(data);
      } catch (err) {
        if (err instanceof DOMException &amp;&amp; err.name === &quot;AbortError&quot;) {
          return; // request was aborted
        }
        setError((err as Error).message);
      } finally {
        setLoading(false);
      }
    };

    fetchUsers();

    // cleanup on unmount
    return () =&gt; {
      controller.abort();
    };
  }, []); // empty dependency array = run once on mount

  if (loading) return &lt;p&gt;Loading...&lt;/p&gt;;
  if (error) return &lt;p&gt;Error: {error}&lt;/p&gt;;

  return (
    &lt;ul&gt;
      {users.map(user =&gt; (
        &lt;li key={user.id}&gt;
          {user.name} ({user.email})
        &lt;/li&gt;
      ))}
    &lt;/ul&gt;
  );
}

export default Users;
</code></pre>

Q: To check whether an application is running using java? A: <pre><code>import java.util.Scanner;

public class AverageOfThreeNumbers {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input three numbers
        System.out.print(&quot;Enter first number: &quot;);
        double a = sc.nextDouble();

        System.out.print(&quot;Enter second number: &quot;);
        double b = sc.nextDouble();

        System.out.print(&quot;Enter third number: &quot;);
        double c = sc.nextDouble();

        // Calculate average
        double average = (a + b + c) / 3;

        // Display result
        System.out.println(&quot;Average = &quot; + average);

        sc.close();
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: Django: User Experience for checking if a person already exists in the database (first and last name, and birthday) A: <p>I ended up doing it like Niko describes.  To share back, here's what I did.</p>
<p>I created an API to query for people's names that sound like the name of someone already in the database (e.g. John and Jon) and an exact match on birthday.  And then I added js to trigger the API and take action (in this case, warn the user that there is a potential duplicate).  One thing I did was extend the Person model to store the sounds_like values to speed up future calls instead of generating it anew each time.</p>
<p>Here's the js</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
  // Wait for the entire page to load before running our code
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    // Get references to the form fields we need to monitor
    const firstNameInput = document.getElementById('id_first_name');
    const lastNameInput = document.getElementById('id_last_name');
    const birthdayInput = document.getElementById('id_birthday');
    const form = document.querySelector('form');

    // Add event listeners to trigger duplicate check when user leaves each field
    // 'blur' = when user clicks away from the field
    // 'change' = when the date value changes
    firstNameInput.addEventListener('blur', checkIfReadyForDuplicateCheck);
    lastNameInput.addEventListener('blur', checkIfReadyForDuplicateCheck);
    birthdayInput.addEventListener('change', checkIfReadyForDuplicateCheck);

    /**
     * Check if all three required fields have values before calling the API
     * This prevents unnecessary API calls when fields are incomplete
     */
    function checkIfReadyForDuplicateCheck() {
      // Get the current values from the form fields
      // .trim() removes any leading/trailing whitespace
      const firstName = firstNameInput.value.trim();
      const lastName = lastNameInput.value.trim();
      const birthday = birthdayInput.value;

      // Only make the API call if all three fields have data
      if (firstName &amp;&amp; lastName &amp;&amp; birthday) {
        checkForDuplicates(firstName, lastName, birthday);
      } else {
        // If any field is empty, remove any existing warning
        clearDuplicateWarning();
      }
    }

    /**
     * Make an API call to check for duplicate students
     * 'async' means this function can use 'await' to wait for the API response
     */
    async function checkForDuplicates(firstName, lastName, birthday) {
      // console.log('Checking for duplicates:', firstName, lastName, birthday);

      // Build the API URL using template literals (backticks)
      // encodeURIComponent() ensures special characters in names are handled safely
      const url = `/client/duplicate-check/student/${encodeURIComponent(firstName)}/${encodeURIComponent(lastName)}/${birthday}/`;
      // console.log('Fetching URL:', url);

      // Get the CSRF token from the hidden form field (Django security requirement)
      const csrfToken = document.querySelector('[name=csrfmiddlewaretoken]').value;

      try {
        // Make the API request
        // 'await' pauses execution until the request completes
        const response = await fetch(url, {
          method: 'GET',
          headers: {
            'Content-Type': 'application/json',
            'X-CSRFToken': csrfToken,  // Include CSRF token for Django
          },
          credentials: 'same-origin',  // Send cookies (for authentication)
        });

        console.log('Response status:', response.status);

        // Parse the JSON response from the API
        const data = await response.json();

        // Check if the response indicates an error (status code 400, 500, etc.)
        if (!response.ok) {
          console.error('Error from API:', data.error);
          return;  // Exit the function early
        }

        console.log('API Response:', data);

        // Check if any duplicates were found
        if (data.duplicate_found &amp;&amp; data.count &gt; 0) {
          console.log(`Found ${data.count} duplicate(s):`, data.results);
          // Show the warning banner with the duplicate data
          showDuplicateWarning(data.results);
        } else {
          console.log('No duplicates found');
          // Clear any existing warning if no duplicates found
          clearDuplicateWarning();
        }

      } catch (error) {
        // Catch any network errors or other exceptions
        console.error('Error checking for duplicates:', error);
      }
    }

    /**
     * Create and display a warning banner showing duplicate students
     * @param {Array} duplicates - Array of student objects from the API
     */
    function showDuplicateWarning(duplicates) {
      // First, remove any existing warning to avoid duplicates
      clearDuplicateWarning();

      // Create a new div element for the warning
      const warningDiv = document.createElement('div');
      warningDiv.id = 'duplicate-warning';  // Give it an ID so we can find it later
      // Add Bootstrap classes for styling: yellow warning box with close button
      warningDiv.className = 'alert alert-warning alert-dismissible fade show';
      warningDiv.setAttribute('role', 'alert');  // Accessibility attribute

      // Determine singular/plural words based on count
      const count = duplicates.length;
      const studentWord = count === 1 ? 'student' : 'students';

      // Build the HTML content for the warning
      // Using template literals (backticks) allows multi-line strings and ${} for variables
      let warningHTML = `
          &lt;h5 class=&quot;alert-heading&quot;&gt;
              &lt;i class=&quot;fa fa-exclamation-triangle&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt; 
                  Potential Duplicate${count &gt; 1 ? 's' : ''} Found
          &lt;/h5&gt;
          &lt;p&gt;
              There are ${count} ${studentWord} with similar names and the same birthday already registered. 
              Is this new student a duplicate of someone already in the system?
          &lt;/p&gt;`;

      // Use ordered list for multiple students, simple paragraph for single
      if (count &gt; 1) {
        // Bootstrap's numbered list component
        warningHTML += '&lt;ol class=&quot;list-group list-group-numbered&quot;&gt;';
        // Loop through each duplicate and add a list item
        duplicates.forEach(dup =&gt; {
          warningHTML += `
        &lt;li class=&quot;list-group-item&quot;&gt;
          &lt;a href=&quot;/client/student/${dup.id}/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;${dup.first_name} ${dup.last_name}&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;/li&gt;
      `;
        });
        warningHTML += '&lt;/ol&gt;';
      } else {
        // Just show a single link if there's only one duplicate
        const dup = duplicates[0];
        warningHTML += `
      &lt;p&gt;
        &lt;a href=&quot;/client/student/${dup.id}/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; class=&quot;fw-bold&quot;&gt;${dup.first_name} ${dup.last_name}&lt;/a&gt;
      &lt;/p&gt;
    `;
      }

      // Add the close button (Bootstrap handles the dismiss functionality automatically)
      warningHTML += `
    &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;btn-close&quot; data-bs-dismiss=&quot;alert&quot; aria-label=&quot;Close&quot;&gt;&lt;/button&gt;
  `;

      // Set the HTML content of our warning div
      warningDiv.innerHTML = warningHTML;

      // Find the form title and insert our warning right after it
      const formTitle = document.querySelector('h5.mt-5.mb-3');
      formTitle.insertAdjacentElement('afterend', warningDiv);

      // Smoothly scroll to show the warning (so user doesn't miss it)
      warningDiv.scrollIntoView({behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest'});
    }

    /**
     * Remove the duplicate warning banner from the page if it exists
     */
    function clearDuplicateWarning() {
      // Try to find an existing warning by its ID
      const existingWarning = document.getElementById('duplicate-warning');
      // If it exists, remove it from the page
      if (existingWarning) {
        existingWarning.remove();
      }
    }
  });
&lt;/script&gt;

</code></pre>
<p>and here's the API view.  I used Jellyfish for the sounds_like function.</p>
<pre><code>class CheckForDuplicates(APIView):
    # permission_classes = [IsAuthenticated]
    authentication_classes = [SessionAuthentication]
    permission_classes = [IsAuthenticated]

    def get(self, request, pt, first, last, dob):
        # Validate person type
        try:
            config = get_person_config(pt)
        except ValueError as e:
            return Response({'error': str(e)}, status=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST)

        # Parse DOB
        try:
            dob_date = datetime.strptime(dob, '%Y-%m-%d').date()
        except ValueError:
            return Response({
                'error': 'Invalid date format. Expected YYYY-MM-DD'
            }, status=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST)

        # Get queryset using the config
        current_user = get_user_from_request(self.request)
        queryset = config['queryset_filter'](current_user.affiliate)

        # Filter by DOB
        filter_kwargs = {config['dob_field']: dob_date}
        all_persons = queryset.filter(**filter_kwargs)

        if config['select_related']:
            all_persons = all_persons.select_related(*config['select_related'])

        # Check for phonetic matches
        first_matcher = SoundsLike(first)
        last_matcher = SoundsLike(last)

        duplicates = [
            person for person in all_persons
            if first_matcher.matches(person.first_name) and last_matcher.matches(person.last_name)
        ]

        if duplicates:
            serializer = config['serializer'](duplicates, many=True)
            return Response({
                'duplicate_found': True,
                'count': len(duplicates),
                'person_type': pt.lower(),
                'results': serializer.data
            }, status=status.HTTP_200_OK)

        return Response({
            'duplicate_found': False,
            'count': 0,
            'person_type': pt.lower(),
            'results': []
        }, status=status.HTTP_200_OK)
</code></pre>
